#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:1
msgid "Support Matrix (preview)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:3
msgid ""
"cute-rs is a **preview**. It compiles Rust CuTe kernels ahead of time "
"through the pinned CUTLASS 4.7 compiler for two targets, `sm_100a` and "
"`sm_120a`, and covers a validated subset of what CuTeDSL 4.7 offers on them. "
"This page lists what the subset holds, what it does not, and what cute-rs "
"adds. Status at commit `5eaa6cbda`, 2026-10-22."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:9
msgid ""
"One glance: CuTeDSL 4.7 across its architectures against the cute-rs preview "
"on its two targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:12
msgid "Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:18
msgid "The two targets the preview compiles for, and the ones it rejects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:0
msgid "Text version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:35
msgid ""
"The target check runs before any MLIR is built, and the error names the "
"target. Within the pair, `tcgen05` operations need `sm_100a` and MXF4 "
"register MMA needs `sm_120a`. `cargo oxide run` uses the detected GPU, so an "
"RTX 5090 gets `sm_120a`; `cargo oxide build` needs `--arch`. Every CuTe "
"kernel needs `CUDA_OXIDE_DEVICE_BACKEND=cutlass-mlir`; the native backend "
"has no CuTe lowering."
msgstr ""

