#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:135
msgid "What cute-rs adds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:137
msgid ""
"Ahead-of-time compilation with no Python runtime: one Rust binary carries "
"the cubin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:138
msgid ""
"Layouts, swizzles, operand roles and pipeline states are Rust types, decoded "
"by the compiler and checked at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:139
msgid ""
"A whole-module verifier runs before any MLIR is built: tensor provenance, "
"pipeline lifecycle, operand roles, TMA encodability and swizzle alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:140
msgid ""
"Two end-to-end models, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B and Qwen3-8B on sm_120a, with "
"reference comparisons. CuTeDSL 4.7 ships component kernels only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:142
msgid "What the compiler does not prove"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:144
msgid ""
"The verifier checks what it can see in types and in the module. These stay "
"with the author at every `unsafe` boundary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:146
msgid "Thread convergence and lane participation at collective operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:147
msgid "Barrier phases and asynchronous completion before a buffer is reused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:148
msgid "Pointer lifetimes behind raw views and descriptors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/support-matrix.md:149
msgid "Disjoint writes across threads."
msgstr ""

